WEBVTT

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.303
DR. MAYA LIN: Greek writers named seven wonders.

00:00:06.323 --> 00:00:09.888
DR. MAYA LIN: Six are gone. Khufu's Great Pyramid
still rises above Giza,

00:00:09.908 --> 00:00:12.718
DR. MAYA LIN: built about four thousand five hundred
years ago.

00:00:13.003 --> 00:00:16.238
DR. MAYA LIN: The question is simple: what did these
builders understand about stone,

00:00:16.258 --> 00:00:17.571
DR. MAYA LIN: weight, and time?

00:00:17.791 --> 00:00:22.149
DR. MAYA LIN: Built for Pharaoh Khufu under royal
vizier and chief architect Hemiunu,

00:00:22.169 --> 00:00:25.561
DR. MAYA LIN: the Great Pyramid stood 146.6 meters
tall —

00:00:25.581 --> 00:00:30.963
DR. MAYA LIN: remaining the tallest human-made
structure on Earth for more than 3,800 years.

00:00:31.248 --> 00:00:35.052
DR. MAYA LIN: Hellenistic scholars chose the number
seven because in classical Greek

00:00:35.072 --> 00:00:38.275
DR. MAYA LIN: cosmology it represented completeness
and perfection:

00:00:38.295 --> 00:00:41.116
DR. MAYA LIN: five known planets plus the Sun and
Moon.

00:00:41.401 --> 00:00:45.755
DR. MAYA LIN: Constructed over roughly twenty to
twenty-seven years during Egypt's Old

00:00:45.775 --> 00:00:49.521
DR. MAYA LIN: Kingdom around 2560 BCE, Khufu's
horizon monument,

00:00:49.541 --> 00:00:53.834
DR. MAYA LIN: originally named Akhet Khufu, crowned
a vast necropolis connected

00:00:53.854 --> 00:00:57.539
DR. MAYA LIN: directly to the Nile via artificial
harbor basins.

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:03.035
DR. MAYA LIN: Far from a single unbroken ribbon,

00:01:03.055 --> 00:01:06.155
DR. MAYA LIN: the Great Wall is an evolutionary
military network

00:01:06.175 --> 00:01:09.649
DR. MAYA LIN: stretching 21,196 kilometers across
deserts,

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:13.580
DR. MAYA LIN: loess plateaus, and knife-edge granite
ridges.

00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:18.443
DR. MAYA LIN: Rival Warring States first raised
stamped-earth ramparts in the seventh

00:01:18.463 --> 00:01:22.264
DR. MAYA LIN: century BCE, which First Emperor Qin
Shi Huang linked

00:01:22.284 --> 00:01:26.927
DR. MAYA LIN: after unifying China in 221 BCE under
general Meng Tian to check nomadic

00:01:26.947 --> 00:01:30.683
DR. MAYA LIN: Xiongnu cavalry raids from the
Eurasian steppe.

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:35.237
DR. MAYA LIN: The iconic crenellated stone-and-brick
dragon clinging to vertical peaks

00:01:35.257 --> 00:01:40.240
DR. MAYA LIN: near Beijing, Jinshanling, and Simatai
dates not to Qin antiquity,

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.933
DR. MAYA LIN: but to the Ming Dynasty after a
disastrous 1449 battle at Tumu

00:01:43.953 --> 00:01:48.102
DR. MAYA LIN: where Oirat Mongols captured the
Zhengtong Emperor himself.

00:01:51.122 --> 00:01:55.562
DR. MAYA LIN: Hidden behind the 1.2-kilometer
tectonic slot gorge of the Siq,

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:59.631
DR. MAYA LIN: Petra was the glittering caravan
capital of the Nabataean Kingdom —

00:01:59.651 --> 00:02:02.920
DR. MAYA LIN: carved top-down into living Paleozoic
sandstone.

00:02:03.205 --> 00:02:07.121
DR. MAYA LIN: Built in under ten years over Emperor
Nero's private artificial lake,

00:02:07.141 --> 00:02:10.794
DR. MAYA LIN: the Flavian Amphitheatre remains the
blueprint for every modern sports

00:02:10.814 --> 00:02:12.263
DR. MAYA LIN: stadium on Earth.

00:02:12.548 --> 00:02:16.463
DR. MAYA LIN: Originally nomadic Arab traders, the
Nabataeans cornered the ancient

00:02:16.483 --> 00:02:19.334
DR. MAYA LIN: world's most lucrative luxury supply
chain.

00:02:19.354 --> 00:02:21.993
DR. MAYA LIN: Frankincense and myrrh from southern
Arabia,

00:02:22.013 --> 00:02:26.140
DR. MAYA LIN: Indian spices, and Dead Sea bitumen
prized by Egypt and Rome.

00:02:26.425 --> 00:02:30.656
DR. MAYA LIN: Following Nero's suicide and the
chaotic Year of the Four Emperors,

00:02:30.676 --> 00:02:34.733
DR. MAYA LIN: General Vespasian launched the
amphitheatre in 70 CE as a masterstroke

00:02:34.753 --> 00:02:38.926
DR. MAYA LIN: of political rehabilitation: draining
Nero's private pleasure lake

00:02:38.946 --> 00:02:43.293
DR. MAYA LIN: in the Domus Aurea to return Rome's
valley center to the public.

00:02:46.313 --> 00:02:50.217
DR. MAYA LIN: Perched on a narrow granite fault
saddle nearly eight thousand feet

00:02:50.237 --> 00:02:53.380
DR. MAYA LIN: above sea level above the raging
Urubamba River,

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.597
DR. MAYA LIN: Machu Picchu is a triumph of
geotechnical and seismic design.

00:02:57.882 --> 00:03:02.172
DR. MAYA LIN: At the center of a vast karst
limestone plain devoid of surface rivers,

00:03:02.192 --> 00:03:04.971
DR. MAYA LIN: Chichén Itzá fused naked-eye Maya
astronomy,

00:03:04.991 --> 00:03:09.224
DR. MAYA LIN: architectural acoustics, and sacred
subterranean hydrology.

00:03:09.509 --> 00:03:14.082
DR. MAYA LIN: Radiocarbon accelerator mass
spectrometry published by Lucy Salazar

00:03:14.102 --> 00:03:18.332
DR. MAYA LIN: and Richard Burger placed Machu
Picchu's construction starting

00:03:18.352 --> 00:03:23.199
DR. MAYA LIN: around 1420–1450 CE as a royal winter
estate for Inca Emperor Pachacuti

00:03:23.219 --> 00:03:27.037
DR. MAYA LIN: after his campaigns down the Urubamba
Valley.

00:03:27.322 --> 00:03:31.195
DR. MAYA LIN: Named for the 'Mouth of the Well of
the Itza,' the metropolis grew

00:03:31.215 --> 00:03:34.114
DR. MAYA LIN: around massive natural sinkholes,
cenotes,

00:03:34.134 --> 00:03:37.682
DR. MAYA LIN: formed where groundwater collapsed
porous limestone resting inside

00:03:37.702 --> 00:03:41.196
DR. MAYA LIN: the outer ring of the Chicxulub
asteroid impact basin.

00:03:44.216 --> 00:03:48.299
DR. MAYA LIN: Commissioned by Mughal Emperor Shah
Jahan for his beloved wife Mumtaz

00:03:48.319 --> 00:03:51.807
DR. MAYA LIN: Mahal, the Taj Mahal marries poetic
grief with daring

00:03:51.827 --> 00:03:56.028
DR. MAYA LIN: seventeenth-century structural and
geotechnical engineering.

00:03:56.313 --> 00:04:00.227
DR. MAYA LIN: Crowning a 710-meter granite pinnacle
battered by Atlantic gales

00:04:00.247 --> 00:04:04.837
DR. MAYA LIN: and tropical lightning, Christ the
Redeemer brings ancient monumental

00:04:04.857 --> 00:04:08.525
DR. MAYA LIN: ambition into the reinforced-concrete
modern era.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:12.977
DR. MAYA LIN: In June 1631, Empress Mumtaz Mahal
died at Burhanpur giving birth

00:04:12.997 --> 00:04:17.046
DR. MAYA LIN: to their fourteenth child;
contemporary court chronicles record

00:04:17.066 --> 00:04:20.526
DR. MAYA LIN: the emperor's beard turned silver
within months.

00:04:20.546 --> 00:04:24.713
DR. MAYA LIN: That lost lineup included Shah Jahan's
trusted political confidante who

00:04:24.733 --> 00:04:27.602
DR. MAYA LIN: accompanied him on military campaigns.

00:04:27.887 --> 00:04:30.278
DR. MAYA LIN: Across millennia of shifting empires,

00:04:30.298 --> 00:04:34.538
DR. MAYA LIN: earthquakes, and desert winds, the 7
Wonders of the World endure

00:04:34.558 --> 00:04:37.453
DR. MAYA LIN: as humanity's boldest signature in
stone.

00:04:37.473 --> 00:04:42.778
DR. MAYA LIN: Proof of what happens when geometry
and imagination refuse to accept the impossible.
